// `jet debug --dap <file.jet>`: the Debug Adapter Protocol over stdio, as an
// editor's launch configuration starts it (VS Code's `debugAdapter`
// executable). Each request is one `Content-Length` framed JSON object on
// stdin; each response and event is one on stdout. The adapter drives the
// NativeSession the `(Jet)` console drives, loaded before the first request,
// so `setBreakpoints` is verified against the image's line table at once.
// `launch` takes `stopOnEntry`, `args` and `stdin`, the file the program
// reads as its standard input (JetCLIDap.stdin_of); the program runs from
// `configurationDone`. `attach` takes `processId`, and `program` when the
// editor names the image that process must run: the session seizes that
// running program, built at O0, where it is, and `configurationDone`
// reports it stopped there. A refusal answers with its registered
// diagnostic, its code as the error's `jetCode`: E2236 for a configuration
// field that is not as it must be (an attach target that is not as given,
// a `showRawFrames` that is not true or false), E2231 when attaching
// failed, E2238 for a frame, scope or variable reference of an earlier
// stop. Run control answers, runs to the next stop and reports it
// (`output` with the program's new output, then `stopped`, or `exited` and
// `terminated`). While the program runs on (`continue`, and its start from
// `configurationDone` or `restart`), the next request stops every thread
// where it is: `pause` reports that stop, except that a program still
// starting, before any code of its own, runs on to the start of its entry
// and stops there, so the stop has a Jet frame; `disconnect` ends the session;
// `restart` starts the program again; a request about a stop (a stack, a
// scope, variables, `evaluate`, `disassemble`) or a run command waits for
// the next stop;
// any other request is answered with the program stopped, which then runs
// on. `restart` takes the launch
// configuration's `stopOnEntry`, `args` and `stdin` again; an attached program does
// not restart. Each task of the program is a thread, by its task id as the
// console's `tasks` lists it, named by its label, its id and its state; the
// `stopped` event names the task the stop is in, which a step steps and
// `evaluate` answers in. A task's frames are its Jet frames: a running
// task's its thread's, a parked task's those its fiber saved when it
// parked; a queued task has none yet. A frame's one scope holds its locals
// as the console shows them, each with its Jet type. Each Jet frame carries
// its pc as its `instructionPointerReference`. `showRawFrames` adds
// the machine frames, each named `[raw]` with its instruction pointer, and
// each its one scope, `[raw] Locals`, of its pc and canonical frame address.
// A frame in Core names its source by a `sourceReference`, and the `source`
// request answers that source's text as the program's Core holds it.
// `disassemble` answers the program's code around a `memoryReference`, as
// jet_debug's NativeListing.jet lists it: each instruction's address, bytes,
// text, the code it is in (`fib+14`; `[debugger]` for the debugger's own,
// a placed condition's or the evaluation room's) and its source line. An
// address no code is known at answers `presentationHint` `invalid`.
// Stepping by instruction and instruction breakpoints are not offered, so
// an editor steps by line from its disassembly view.
// A frame id or variable reference names the stop it was made at; once the
// program runs again, it names nothing.
// A breakpoint may carry a `condition` and a `logMessage`, and `evaluate`
// answers an expression in a paused frame, all through the debugger's one
// evaluator, the compiler (DebugCompile.jet, jet_debug's NativeEval.jet). The
// session settles each run as the `(Jet)` console does: a hit whose
// condition is false, or a logpoint's hit (which logs its message), does not
// stop: a continue runs on, and a step goes on to where it would have
// stopped.
// In a replay (`jet debug --dap --replay=NAME`) the adapter answers
// `supportsStepBack`: `stepBack` and `reverseContinue` run the session's
// `reverse-next` and `reverse-continue`, and report where they stopped as
// a step does. A replay's runs are made as recorded, so a request waits for
// them. Going back outside a replay, after `fix`, or where the replay holds
// nothing earlier is refused with E2237 (the last at the same stop, whose
// frame ids still hold). A replay refused before its session began (a
// recording of other source, E3621) answers every request with that
// refusal (jet_cli_dap_refused). `jump` ({"event": N}), `back`
// ({"count": K}, optional) and `events`, requests of Jet's own, are the
// console's: `jump` and `back` answer with the event they go to and
// report its stop with reason `goto`; `events` answers with the replay's
// history, each event's `event`, `reason`, `function`, `file` and `line`
// and whether it is `current`.
// `dataBreakpointInfo` and `setDataBreakpoints` are the console's `watch`:
// a local or a field path of a frame of the stopped task, which stops at
// each write that changes it, reported as a `data breakpoint` stop whose
// description is the change (`total: 0 -> 2`). A place no watch can take
// has no data id; its description is E2237's What.
// `fix`, a request of Jet's own, is the console's `fix`: the program's
// source is compiled again as its build compiled it and each function the
// edit changed is swapped into the stopped program (DebugFix.jet). It
// answers with what the console would show (`Fixed ...`, or `Nothing to
// fix ...`) as the response's `message`; a refused fix fails with why, and
// the program runs on as it was.
// `disconnect` ends a launched program and lets an attached one go on, then
// ends the adapter, as the end of stdin does at a stop. The end of stdin
// while a launched program runs on stops no run: the program runs on to its
// next stop or its end, which is reported, and the requests that wait for a
// stop are answered there; then the session ends.
use {
    dap_files: core.files
    dap_json: core.encoding.json
    dap_term: core.term
    jet_debug.[NATIVE_ATTACH_INVALID, NATIVE_DEBUG_REFUSED, NATIVE_DEBUG_TASK_RUNNING, NativeDebugError, NativeEvalRefused, NativeListedRow, NativeLocal, NativeSaid, NativeSession, NativeSettled, NativeStop, NativeStopKind, NativeWatched, native_debug_hex, native_debug_jet_frame, native_debug_report, native_debug_rule_place, native_function_at, native_listing_bytes, native_listing_window, native_lookup]
    jet_foundation.[DeepChecks, Diagnostic, MODULE_CORE_PREFIX, diagnostic_from_registry, foundation_json_integer, foundation_json_quote]
}

// One `setBreakpoints` entry: its line, and its condition and log message
// ("" for none).
JetCLIDapBreakpoint: struct {
    line: Int,
    condition: String,
    log: String,
}

// One request: its sequence number, its command and its arguments' members.
JetCLIDapRequest: struct {
    seq: Int,
    command: String,
    arguments: [{key: String, value: Dyn}],
}

// A frame a `stackTrace` listed at this stop: its task, and its index in
// that task's backtrace, a machine frame's from JET_CLI_DAP_RAW.
JetCLIDapFrame: struct {
    task: Int,
    index: Int,
}

// A watch `setDataBreakpoints` placed: its data id (dataBreakpointInfo's)
// and the session's number for it.
JetCLIDapWatch: struct {
    id: String,
    number: Int,
}

// E2238: a frame, scope or variable reference of an earlier stop.
JET_CLI_DAP_STALE: "E2238"

// A frame id is its stop's number (JetCLIDap.stops) above its row among the
// frames this stop's `stackTrace` answers listed (JetCLIDap.frames), in the
// low JET_CLI_DAP_FRAME_BITS bits. Stop numbers wrap at JET_CLI_DAP_STOPS,
// which keeps every variable reference (twice a frame id, plus 1 or 2)
// below 2^31, as DAP asks.
JET_CLI_DAP_FRAME_BITS: 16

// The machine frames `showRawFrames` adds are indexed from here in their
// task's frames.
JET_CLI_DAP_RAW: 32768

JET_CLI_DAP_STOPS: 8192

// The most instructions one `disassemble` answers.
JET_CLI_DAP_MOST_INSTRUCTIONS: 65536

// The adapter's state across requests.
JetCLIDap: struct {
    // The last message's sequence number.
    seq: Int,
    stop_on_entry: Bool,
    args: [String],
    // The breakpoints each source file's `setBreakpoints` placed; the
    // session keeps their conditions and log messages.
    placed: [String:[Int]],
    launched: Bool,
    // Whether `attach` took the program, whose stop `configurationDone`
    // has yet to report.
    attached: Bool{false},
    // The number of the stop the program is at, which its frame ids and
    // variable references name.
    stops: Int{0},
    // The frames this stop's `stackTrace` answers listed, which its frame
    // ids name by row, and each one's row by its task and index
    // (jet_cli_dap_frame_key).
    frames: [JetCLIDapFrame]{[JetCLIDapFrame]{}},
    rows: [Int:Int]{[Int:Int]{}},
    // The task the program stopped in.
    task: Int{1},
    // Whether the session ended (`disconnect`, or the end of stdin).
    done: Bool{false},
    // The requests that came while the program ran, which wait for its
    // next stop, in the order they came.
    waiting: [JetCLIDapRequest]{[JetCLIDapRequest]{}},
    // Whether stdin ended while the program ran: no request stops a run any
    // more, and the session ends at the next stop.
    ended: Bool{false},
    // The watches `setDataBreakpoints` placed.
    data: [JetCLIDapWatch]{[JetCLIDapWatch]{}},
    // Whether `fix` has the program's source: a built image's build is
    // not known, so `fix` refuses it.
    fixable: Bool{false},
    // The Core sources `stackTrace` named, each by its `sourceReference`,
    // its index plus 1, which the `source` request reads.
    sources: [String]{[String]{}},

    handle: fn(&self, session: &NativeSession, input: &&JetCLIDapRequest, entry: String, deep_checks: DeepChecks) -[FS, Env, Exec, IO, Net, Time, FFI.Asm]> Never! {
        request := input.move()
        // Another task's frames are read within the request that names them.
        session.focus = None
        if request.command == {
            "initialize" -> {
                back: if session.replaying() -> ",\"supportsStepBack\":true" else -> ""
                self.respond(request, "{{\"supportsConfigurationDoneRequest\":true,\"supportsConditionalBreakpoints\":true,\"supportsLogPoints\":true,\"supportsEvaluateForHovers\":true,\"supportsRestartRequest\":true,\"supportsDataBreakpoints\":true,\"supportsDisassembleRequest\":true{back}}}")
            }
            "launch" -> {
                session.input_path = self.stdin_of(request, request.arguments) ?? return
                self.stop_on_entry = jet_cli_dap_bool(request.arguments, "stopOnEntry")
                self.args = jet_cli_dap_texts_of(request.arguments.move(), "args")
                request.arguments = [{key: String, value: Dyn}]{}
                self.respond(request, "{{}}")
                self.event("initialized", "{{}}")
            }
            "attach" -> {
                if self.launched -> return self.fail(request, "the session already has its program")
                if session.attach(jet_cli_dap_int(request.arguments, "processId"), jet_cli_dap_string(request.arguments, "program")) == {
                    .Ok(_) -> {
                        self.launched = true
                        self.attached = true
                        self.respond(request, "{{}}")
                        self.event("initialized", "{{}}")
                    }
                    .Err(refused) -> self.refuse(request, refused.code, refused.detail)
                }
            }
            "setBreakpoints" -> {
                if self.set_breakpoints(session, request) == {
                    .Ok(body) -> { self.respond(request, body) }
                    .Err(failure) -> self.fail(request, failure.detail)
                }
            }
            "configurationDone" -> {
                self.respond(request, "{{}}")
                if self.attached {
                    self.attached = false
                    return self.report(session, NativeSettled{stop: NativeStop{kind: NativeStopKind.Paused, reason: "attach", code: 0, frame: None}, hit: None, said: [NativeSaid]{}}, "pause")
                }
                if self.launched {
                    return
                }
                self.launched = true
                self.run_on(session, "", entry, deep_checks)
            }
            "restart" -> {
                if session.attached {
                    return self.fail(request, "an attached program does not restart; disconnect and attach again")
                }
                // The launch configuration the editor restarts with.
                config := jet_cli_dap_object_of(request.arguments.move(), "arguments")
                request.arguments = [{key: String, value: Dyn}]{}
                if config.len() > 0 {
                    session.input_path = self.stdin_of(request, config) ?? return
                    self.stop_on_entry = jet_cli_dap_bool(config, "stopOnEntry")
                    self.args = jet_cli_dap_texts_of(config.move(), "args")
                }
                self.respond(request, "{{}}")
                // Before `configurationDone`, which starts it, there is no
                // run to start again.
                if !self.launched {
                    return
                }
                self.run_on(session, "", entry, deep_checks)
            }
            "pause" -> {
                // A program not running is paused already.
                self.respond(request, "{{}}")
            }
            "threads" -> {
                if !self.launched || !session.alive() {
                    return self.respond(request, "{{\"threads\":[{{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"run\"}}]}}")
                }
                if jet_cli_dap_threads(session) == {
                    .Ok(body) -> { self.respond(request, body) }
                    .Err(failure) -> self.fail(request, failure.detail)
                }
            }
            "stackTrace" -> {
                if !self.launched || !session.alive() {
                    return self.fail(request, "the program is not paused")
                }
                raw := false
                loop member in request.arguments {
                    if member.key != "showRawFrames" -> next
                    if member.value == .Bool(flag) {
                        raw = flag
                        next
                    }
                    return self.refuse(request, NATIVE_ATTACH_INVALID, "field showRawFrames must be true or false")
                }
                asked: jet_cli_dap_int(request.arguments, "threadId")
                if self.stack(session, if asked > 0 -> asked else -> self.task, raw) == {
                    .Ok(body) -> { self.respond(request, body) }
                    .Err(failure) -> self.fail(request, failure.detail)
                }
            }
            "scopes" -> {
                if !self.launched || !session.alive() {
                    return self.fail(request, "the program is not paused")
                }
                id: jet_cli_dap_int(request.arguments, "frameId")
                frame: self.frame_of(id) ?? return self.refuse(request, JET_CLI_DAP_STALE, "reference {id} expired when execution resumed")
                scope: if frame.index >= JET_CLI_DAP_RAW -> "{{\"name\":\"[raw] Locals\",\"presentationHint\":\"registers\",\"variablesReference\":{id * 2 + 2},\"expensive\":false}}" else -> "{{\"name\":\"Locals\",\"presentationHint\":\"locals\",\"variablesReference\":{id * 2 + 1},\"expensive\":false}}"
                self.respond(request, "{{\"scopes\":[{scope}]}}")
            }
            "variables" -> {
                if !self.launched || !session.alive() {
                    return self.fail(request, "the program is not paused")
                }
                reference: jet_cli_dap_int(request.arguments, "variablesReference")
                if reference <= 0 -> return self.respond(request, "{{\"variables\":[]}}")
                // A scope's reference is twice its frame's id, plus 1 for
                // Locals and 2 for `[raw] Locals`.
                frame: self.frame_of((reference - 1) >> 1) ?? return self.refuse(request, JET_CLI_DAP_STALE, "reference {reference} expired when execution resumed")
                if self.focus(session, frame.task) == {
                    .Ok(found) -> {
                        if !found {
                            return self.fail(request, "task {frame.task} has no frames at this stop")
                        }
                    }
                    .Err(failure) -> return self.fail(request, failure.detail)
                }
                if jet_cli_dap_variables(session, frame.index) == {
                    .Ok(body) -> { self.respond(request, body) }
                    .Err(failure) -> self.fail(request, failure.detail)
                }
            }
            "evaluate" -> {
                if !self.launched || !session.alive() {
                    return self.fail(request, "the program is not paused")
                }
                // No frame names the stopped task's innermost.
                id: jet_cli_dap_int(request.arguments, "frameId")
                index := 0
                if id >= 0 {
                    frame: self.frame_of(id) ?? return self.refuse(request, JET_CLI_DAP_STALE, "reference {id} expired when execution resumed")
                    if frame.task != self.task {
                        return self.fail(request, "`evaluate` answers in task {self.task}, where the program stopped; task {frame.task}'s values are its frames' Variables")
                    }
                    index = frame.index
                }
                if index >= JET_CLI_DAP_RAW {
                    return self.fail(request, "a raw frame has no Jet locals to evaluate with; choose a Jet frame")
                }
                if jet_cli_dap_evaluate(session, jet_cli_dap_string(request.arguments, "expression"), index) == {
                    .Ok(body) -> { self.respond(request, body) }
                    .Err(failure) -> self.fail(request, failure.message)
                }
            }
            "continue" | "next" | "stepIn" | "stepOut" -> {
                if !self.launched || !session.alive() {
                    return self.fail(request, "the program is not paused")
                }
                asked: jet_cli_dap_int(request.arguments, "threadId")
                if request.command != "continue" && asked > 0 && asked != self.task {
                    return self.fail(request, "a step steps task {self.task}, where the program stopped, not task {asked}")
                }
                self.respond(request, if request.command == "continue" -> "{{\"allThreadsContinued\":true}}" else -> "{{}}")
                word: if request.command == {
                    "continue" -> "c"
                    "next" -> "n"
                    "stepIn" -> "s"
                    else -> "f"
                }
                self.run_on(session, word, entry, deep_checks)
            }
            "stepBack" | "reverseContinue" -> {
                if !self.launched || !session.alive() {
                    return self.fail(request, "the program is not paused")
                }
                refusal: session.reverse_refusal()
                if refusal != "" -> return self.refuse(request, NATIVE_DEBUG_REFUSED, refusal)
                word: if request.command == "stepBack" -> "n" else -> "c"
                if session.reverse(word) == {
                    .Ok(stop) -> {
                        // Why it stopped where it did, when that says more.
                        if session.notes != "" {
                            self.event("output", "{{\"category\":\"console\",\"output\":{foundation_json_quote(session.notes)}}}")
                            session.notes = ""
                        }
                        // Nothing earlier: the program is back at this
                        // stop, whose frame ids still hold.
                        if session.nowhere != "" {
                            return self.refuse(request, NATIVE_DEBUG_REFUSED, session.nowhere)
                        }
                        self.respond(request, "{{}}")
                        self.report(session, stop, if word == "c" -> "pause" else -> "step")
                    }
                    .Err(failure) -> {
                        self.respond(request, "{{}}")
                        self.stopped_by(failure)
                    }
                }
            }
            "jump" | "back" -> {
                if !self.launched || !session.alive() {
                    return self.fail(request, "the program is not paused")
                }
                refusal: session.replay_refusal("`{request.command}`")
                if refusal != "" -> return self.refuse(request, NATIVE_DEBUG_REFUSED, refusal)
                latest: session.latest_event()
                event := jet_cli_dap_int(request.arguments, "event")
                if request.command == "jump" && (event < 0 || event > latest) {
                    return self.fail(request, "`jump` needs an event, 0 to {latest}")
                }
                if request.command == "back" {
                    count: jet_cli_dap_int(request.arguments, "count")
                    event = session.back_event(if count < 0 -> 0 else -> count) ?? {
                        nothing: if count <= 0 && session.watches.len() > 0 -> "the replay holds no stop at a watch before this one" else -> "the replay holds no event that far back"
                        return self.refuse(request, NATIVE_DEBUG_REFUSED, nothing)
                    }
                }
                if session.jump(event) == {
                    .Ok(stop) -> {
                        if session.notes != "" {
                            self.event("output", "{{\"category\":\"console\",\"output\":{foundation_json_quote(session.notes)}}}")
                            session.notes = ""
                        }
                        self.respond(request, "{{\"event\":{event}}}")
                        self.report(session, stop, "goto")
                    }
                    .Err(failure) -> {
                        self.respond(request, "{{}}")
                        self.stopped_by(failure)
                    }
                }
            }
            "events" -> {
                if !self.launched || !session.alive() {
                    return self.fail(request, "the program is not paused")
                }
                refusal: session.replay_refusal("`events`")
                if refusal != "" -> return self.refuse(request, NATIVE_DEBUG_REFUSED, refusal)
                current: session.moves.len() - 2
                rows := [String]{}
                loop (index, made) in session.moves {
                    if index > 0 {
                        rows.push(jet_cli_dap_event(index - 1, made.reached, current: index - 1 == current))
                    }
                }
                loop step in 0..<session.ahead.len() {
                    rows.push(jet_cli_dap_event(current + 1 + step, session.ahead[session.ahead.len() - 1 - step].reached))
                }
                self.respond(request, "{{\"events\":[{rows.join(",")}]}}")
            }
            "dataBreakpointInfo" -> {
                if !self.launched || !session.alive() {
                    return self.fail(request, "the program is not paused")
                }
                // A scope's reference names its frame (`variables`); with
                // neither it nor a frame id, the stopped task's innermost.
                reference: jet_cli_dap_int(request.arguments, "variablesReference")
                id: if reference > 0 -> (reference - 1) >> 1 else -> jet_cli_dap_int(request.arguments, "frameId")
                index := 0
                if id >= 0 {
                    named: if reference > 0 -> reference else -> id
                    frame: self.frame_of(id) ?? return self.refuse(request, JET_CLI_DAP_STALE, "reference {named} expired when execution resumed")
                    if frame.task != self.task {
                        return self.respond(request, jet_cli_dap_no_data("a watch watches a frame of task {self.task}, where the program stopped, not of task {frame.task}"))
                    }
                    index = frame.index
                }
                if index >= JET_CLI_DAP_RAW {
                    return self.respond(request, jet_cli_dap_no_data("a raw frame has no Jet locals to watch; choose a Jet frame"))
                }
                name: jet_cli_dap_string(request.arguments, "name")
                if jet_cli_dap_watch(session, name, index, place: false) == {
                    .Ok(found) -> {
                        if found.refused != "" {
                            return self.respond(request, jet_cli_dap_no_data(found.refused))
                        }
                        self.respond(request, "{{\"dataId\":{foundation_json_quote("{self.stops}:{index}:{name}")},\"description\":{foundation_json_quote(name)},\"accessTypes\":[\"write\"],\"canPersist\":false}}")
                    }
                    .Err(failure) -> self.fail(request, failure.detail)
                }
            }
            "setDataBreakpoints" -> {
                if self.set_data(session, request) == {
                    .Ok(body) -> { self.respond(request, body) }
                    .Err(failure) -> self.fail(request, failure.detail)
                }
            }
            "source" -> {
                reference: jet_cli_dap_int(request.arguments, "sourceReference")
                if reference < 1 || reference > self.sources.len() {
                    return self.fail(request, "no source has reference {reference}")
                }
                path: "{self.sources[reference - 1]}"
                text: session.source_text(path) ?? return self.fail(request, err.detail)
                self.respond(request, "{{\"content\":{foundation_json_quote(text)}}}")
            }
            "disassemble" -> {
                if !self.launched || !session.alive() {
                    return self.fail(request, "the program is not paused")
                }
                reference: jet_cli_dap_string(request.arguments, "memoryReference")
                address: jet_cli_dap_address(reference) ?? return self.refuse(request, NATIVE_ATTACH_INVALID, "field memoryReference must be an address, as 0x401000")
                count: jet_cli_dap_int(request.arguments, "instructionCount")
                if count < 0 || count > JET_CLI_DAP_MOST_INSTRUCTIONS {
                    return self.refuse(request, NATIVE_ATTACH_INVALID, "field instructionCount must be from 0 to {JET_CLI_DAP_MOST_INSTRUCTIONS}")
                }
                at: address + jet_cli_dap_offset(request.arguments, "offset")
                rows := [String]{}
                loop row in native_listing_window(session, at, jet_cli_dap_offset(request.arguments, "instructionOffset"), count) {
                    rows.push(self.instruction(session, row))
                }
                self.respond(request, "{{\"instructions\":[{rows.join(",")}]}}")
            }
            "fix" -> {
                if !self.launched || !session.alive() {
                    return self.fail(request, "the program is not paused")
                }
                if !self.fixable {
                    return self.fail(request, "fix needs the program's source: debug it as `jet debug --dap <file.jet>`")
                }
                said: jet_cli_debug_fix(session, entry, deep_checks, false).trim_end()
                if !said.starts_with("Fixed") && !said.starts_with("Nothing to fix") {
                    return self.fail(request, said)
                }
                self.respond(request, "{{\"message\":{foundation_json_quote(said)}}}")
            }
            else -> self.fail(request, "`jet debug --dap` does not answer `{request.command}`")
        }
    }

    // `setBreakpoints`: the source's breakpoints become the requested lines,
    // each with its condition and log message, compiled where it traps. One
    // whose condition or message doesn't compile there is not placed.
    set_breakpoints: fn(&self, session: &NativeSession, request: JetCLIDapRequest) -[FS, Env, Exec, IO, Net, Time, FFI.Asm]> String NativeDebugError! {
        file := ""
        specs := [JetCLIDapBreakpoint]{}
        loop member in request.arguments {
            if member.key == "source" && member.value == .Object(source) {
                loop part in source {
                    if part.key == "path" && part.value == .Text(path) {
                        file = dap_files.basename(path)
                    }
                }
            }
            if member.key == "breakpoints" && member.value == .Array(items) {
                loop item in items {
                    if item == .Object(spec) {
                        specs.push(JetCLIDapBreakpoint{line: jet_cli_dap_int(spec, "line"), condition: jet_cli_dap_string(spec, "condition"), log: jet_cli_dap_string(spec, "logMessage")})
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        old: self.placed.get(file) ?? [Int]{}
        loop number in old { session.delete_breakpoint(number) ?? return Err(err) }
        numbers := [Int]{}
        rows := [String]{}
        loop spec in specs {
            line: spec.line
            placed := -1
            if file != "" && line >= 1 {
                if session.break_at(file, line) == {
                    .Ok(found) -> placed = found ?? -1
                    .Err(failure) -> return Err(failure)
                }
            }
            if placed < 0 {
                rows.push("{{\"verified\":false,\"line\":{line},\"message\":{foundation_json_quote("No code on {file}:{line}")}}}")
                next
            }
            reason := ""
            if spec.condition.trim() != "" || spec.log != "" {
                if session.make_rule(placed, spec.condition, spec.log, "break {file}:{line}") == {
                    .Ok(rule) -> { reason = session.set_rule(placed, rule) }
                    .Err(refused) -> {
                        session.take_back(placed) ?? return Err(err)
                        rows.push("{{\"verified\":false,\"line\":{line},\"message\":{foundation_json_quote(refused.message)}}}")
                        next
                    }
                }
            }
            numbers.push(placed)
            place: native_debug_rule_place(spec.condition, spec.log, reason)
            note: if place == "" -> "" else -> ",\"message\":{foundation_json_quote(place.trim())}"
            rows.push("{{\"id\":{placed},\"verified\":true,\"line\":{line}{note}}}")
        }
        self.placed[file.move()] = numbers.move()
        Ok("{{\"breakpoints\":[{rows.join(",")}]}}")
    }

    // `setDataBreakpoints`: the watches become those the request's data ids
    // name (dataBreakpointInfo's `<stop>:<frame>:<name>`). A watch placed
    // for an id before stays as it was set; the others go. A new id is
    // placed in its frame, which must be of this stop (E2238's What
    // otherwise); one no watch can take is not verified, with E2237's What.
    // Each refusal's `jetCode` names its code.
    set_data: fn(&self, session: &NativeSession, request: JetCLIDapRequest) -[FS, Env, Exec, IO, Net, Time, FFI.Asm]> String NativeDebugError! {
        ids := [String]{}
        loop member in request.arguments {
            if member.key == "breakpoints" && member.value == .Array(items) {
                loop item in items {
                    if item == .Object(spec) -> ids.push(jet_cli_dap_string(spec, "dataId"))
                }
            }
        }
        live: self.launched && session.alive()
        // Each id's watch placed before, or -1.
        numbers := [Int]{}
        loop id in ids {
            kept := -1
            loop watch in self.data {
                if live && watch.id == id && session.has_breakpoint(watch.number) {
                    kept = watch.number
                }
            }
            numbers.push(kept)
        }
        loop watch in self.data {
            if live && !numbers.contains(watch.number) && session.has_breakpoint(watch.number) {
                session.delete_breakpoint(watch.number) ?? return Err(err)
            }
        }
        self.data = [JetCLIDapWatch]{}
        rows := [String]{}
        ids.reverse()
        numbers.reverse()
        loop ids.len() > 0 {
            id: ids.pop() ?? break
            number := numbers.pop() ?? -1
            if number < 0 {
                if !live {
                    rows.push("{{\"verified\":false,\"message\":\"the program is not paused\"}}")
                    next
                }
                at: jet_cli_dap_data_place(id)
                if at.stop != self.stops || at.index < 0 || at.index >= JET_CLI_DAP_RAW {
                    rows.push(jet_cli_dap_unverified(JET_CLI_DAP_STALE, "data id `{id}` expired when execution resumed"))
                    next
                }
                placed: jet_cli_dap_watch(session, at.name, at.index) ?? return Err(err)
                if placed.refused != "" {
                    rows.push(jet_cli_dap_unverified(NATIVE_DEBUG_REFUSED, placed.refused))
                    next
                }
                number = placed.number
            }
            rows.push("{{\"id\":{number},\"verified\":true}}")
            self.data.push(JetCLIDapWatch{id: id, number: number})
        }
        Ok("{{\"breakpoints\":[{rows.join(",")}]}}")
    }

    // Run the program as the console run command `word` says, or, for "",
    // as `configurationDone` does: from its start, to the start of its
    // entry (NativeSession.program_entry) under `stopOnEntry`.
    start: fn(&self, session: &NativeSession, word: String) -[FS, Env, Exec, IO, Net, Time, FFI.Asm]> NativeSettled NativeDebugError! {
        if word != "" -> return session.run(word)
        if !self.stop_on_entry {
            first: session.launch(self.args) ?? return Err(err)
            return session.settle_launch(first)
        }
        entry := -1
        if session.break_in_entry() == {
            .Ok(found) -> entry = found ?? -1
            .Err(failure) -> return Err(failure)
        }
        stop: session.launch(self.args) ?? return Err(err)
        if entry >= 0 -> session.delete_breakpoint(entry) ?? return Err(err)
        Ok(NativeSettled{stop: stop, hit: None, said: [NativeSaid]{}})
    }

    // Run a program that a pause found still starting (jet_cli_dap_starting)
    // on to the start of its entry, the Jet function its image's `main`
    // hands the run to (NativeSession.program_entry), so the pause's stop
    // has the program's first Jet frame. A breakpoint the program reaches
    // first, or its end, is the stop instead. None when the image names no
    // entry.
    to_start: fn(&self, session: &NativeSession) -[FS, Env, Exec, IO, Net, Time, FFI.Asm]> NativeSettled? NativeDebugError! {
        number := -1
        if session.break_in_entry() == {
            .Ok(found) -> number = found ?? return Ok(None)
            .Err(failure) -> return Err(failure)
        }
        reached := session.run("c") ?? return Err(err)
        session.delete_breakpoint(number) ?? return Err(err)
        if (reached.hit ?? -1) == number -> reached.hit = None
        Ok(Val(reached))
    }

    // Run the program as `word` says (a console run command, or "" to
    // start it as `configurationDone` does) and report where it stopped. A
    // continue, or a start that does not stop on entry, stops every thread
    // where it is when a request comes (NativeSession.interrupt, on stdin):
    // `pause` reports that stop; `disconnect` ends the session, as the end
    // of stdin does for an attached program no request waits on, while a
    // launched one runs on to its next stop after it; `restart` starts the
    // program again; a request about a stop or a run command waits for the
    // next stop (JetCLIDap.waiting); any other request is answered, and the
    // program continues. A replay's runs are made as recorded, without
    // stopping for requests.
    run_on: fn(&self, session: &NativeSession, word: String, entry: String, deep_checks: DeepChecks) -[FS, Env, Exec, IO, Net, Time, FFI.Asm]> Never! {
        how := word
        loop {
            starting: how == ""
            reason := "step"
            if how == "c" || starting -> reason = "pause"
            if starting && self.stop_on_entry -> reason = "entry"
            // A start that stops on entry is not stopped early: its entry
            // breakpoint goes when the launch stops.
            resumes: how == "c" || (starting && !self.stop_on_entry)
            if resumes && !session.replaying() && !self.ended -> session.interrupt = 0
            outcome := NativeSettled?{None}
            if self.start(session, how) == {
                .Ok(stop) -> { outcome = Val(stop) }
                .Err(failure) -> {
                    session.interrupt = -1
                    return self.stopped_by(failure)
                }
            }
            session.interrupt = -1
            settled := outcome ?? return
            if !session.interrupted -> return self.report(session, settled, reason)
            // What the run said before the request stopped it.
            self.tell(session, settled.said)
            how = "c"
            read: jet_cli_dap_read()
            if read == None {
                if session.attached && self.waiting.len() == 0 -> return self.end(session)
                // A launched program runs on to its next stop or its end,
                // which the waiting requests are answered at.
                self.ended = true
                next
            }
            request: jet_cli_dap_request(read)
            if request.command == {
                "pause" -> {
                    self.respond(request, "{{}}")
                    settled.said = [NativeSaid]{}
                    if (jet_cli_dap_starting(session) ?? return self.stopped_by(err)) {
                        if self.to_start(session) == {
                            .Ok(reached) -> {
                                if reached.move() == .Val(found) -> settled = found
                            }
                            .Err(failure) -> return self.stopped_by(failure)
                        }
                    }
                    return self.report(session, settled, "pause")
                }
                "disconnect" -> {
                    self.end(session)
                    return self.respond(request, "{{}}")
                }
                "restart" -> {
                    attached: session.attached
                    self.handle(session, request.move(), entry, deep_checks)
                    // An attached program, which does not restart, runs on.
                    if !attached {
                        return
                    }
                }
                "stackTrace" | "scopes" | "variables" | "evaluate" | "disassemble" | "continue" | "next" | "stepIn" | "stepOut" | "stepBack" | "reverseContinue" | "jump" | "back" | "events" -> {
                    self.waiting.push(request.move())
                }
                else -> self.handle(session, request.move(), entry, deep_checks)
            }
        }
    }

    // The end of the session: a launched program ends, an attached one
    // goes on (NativeSession.close).
    end: fn(&self, session: &NativeSession) Never! {
        session.close()
        self.done = true
    }

    // `stackTrace` of task `task` at this stop: its Jet frames, innermost
    // first, each by its row in `frames`, which `scopes`, `variables` and
    // `evaluate` name it by, with the pc `disassemble` lists its code from;
    // with `raw`, then its machine frames. A task with no stack yet (a
    // queued one) has none.
    stack: fn(&self, session: &NativeSession, task: Int, raw: Bool) -> String NativeDebugError! {
        if !(self.focus(session, task) ?? return Err(err)) {
            return Ok("{{\"stackFrames\":[],\"totalFrames\":0}}")
        }
        frames: session.backtrace() ?? return Err(err)
        rows := [String]{}
        loop (index, frame) in frames {
            if !native_debug_jet_frame(frame) -> next
            id: self.frame_id(task, index) ?? return Err(NativeDebugError{detail: "this stop's frames outnumber the frame ids a stop has"})
            source: self.source(session, frame.file, frame.path)
            // A caller's frame at a call with a call-site row names the
            // call's column; any other frame its line.
            column: if frame.column > 0 -> frame.column else -> 1
            pointer: if frame.pc > 0 -> ",\"instructionPointerReference\":\"{native_debug_hex(frame.pc)}\"" else -> ""
            rows.push("{{\"id\":{id},\"name\":{foundation_json_quote(frame.function)},\"source\":{source},\"line\":{frame.line},\"column\":{column}{pointer}}}")
        }
        if raw {
            machine: session.unwind() ?? return Err(err)
            loop (index, frame) in machine {
                id: self.frame_id(task, JET_CLI_DAP_RAW + index) ?? return Err(NativeDebugError{detail: "this stop's frames outnumber the frame ids a stop has"})
                function: if native_function_at(session.image, native_lookup(index, frame.pc)) == .Val(found) -> found.name else -> "?"
                rows.push("{{\"id\":{id},\"name\":{foundation_json_quote("[raw] {function}")},\"line\":0,\"column\":0,\"instructionPointerReference\":\"{native_debug_hex(frame.pc)}\",\"presentationHint\":\"subtle\"}}")
            }
        }
        Ok("{{\"stackFrames\":[{rows.join(",")}],\"totalFrames\":{rows.len()}}}")
    }

    // The DAP source of the file `file` (as the line table names it) whose
    // source is `path` (native_line_source): the file the session reads it
    // from (NativeSession.source_file), else `path` itself, made absolute.
    // A Core source is no file: the `source` request reads it by its
    // `sourceReference` (NativeSession.source_text).
    source: fn(&self, session: &NativeSession, file: String, path: String) -> String Never! {
        name: foundation_json_quote(dap_files.basename(file))
        if path.starts_with(MODULE_CORE_PREFIX) {
            return "{{\"name\":{name},\"path\":{foundation_json_quote(path)},\"sourceReference\":{self.source_reference(path)}}}"
        }
        found: session.source_file(path) ?? path
        "{{\"name\":{name},\"path\":{foundation_json_quote(dap_files.resolve(found) ?? found)}}}"
    }

    // One instruction `disassemble` answers: its address, bytes, text and
    // the code it is in, its source and line when its function has them;
    // an address no code is known at is `invalid`, as DAP asks.
    instruction: fn(&self, session: &NativeSession, row: NativeListedRow) -> String Never! {
        address: native_debug_hex(row.address)
        if !row.valid {
            return "{{\"address\":\"{address}\",\"instruction\":\"(no code)\",\"presentationHint\":\"invalid\"}}"
        }
        symbol: if row.symbol == "" -> "" else -> ",\"symbol\":{foundation_json_quote(row.symbol)}"
        place: if row.line > 0 && row.file != "" -> ",\"location\":{self.source(session, row.file, row.path)},\"line\":{row.line}" else -> ""
        "{{\"address\":\"{address}\",\"instructionBytes\":\"{native_listing_bytes(row.bytes)}\",\"instruction\":{foundation_json_quote(row.text)}{symbol}{place}}}"
    }

    // Read task `task`'s frames (NativeSession.focus_task) unless the
    // program stopped in it; false when it has no stack.
    focus: fn(self, session: &NativeSession, task: Int) -> Bool NativeDebugError! {
        session.focus = None
        if task == self.task -> return Ok(true)
        session.focus_task(task)
    }

    // The `sourceReference` of the Core source `path`: its index in
    // `sources` plus 1, added when first named.
    source_reference: fn(&self, path: String) -> Int Never! {
        loop (index, named) in self.sources {
            if named == path -> return index + 1
        }
        self.sources.push("{path}")
        self.sources.len()
    }

    // The id of task `task`'s frame `index` at this stop: its row in
    // `frames`, added when first listed. None once the rows fill the frame
    // id's low bits.
    frame_id: fn(&self, task: Int, index: Int) -> Int? Never! {
        key: jet_cli_dap_frame_key(task, index)
        row: self.rows.get(key) ?? {
            if self.frames.len() >= 1 << JET_CLI_DAP_FRAME_BITS -> return None
            added: self.frames.len()
            self.frames.push(JetCLIDapFrame{task: task, index: index})
            self.rows[key] = added
            added
        }
        Val((self.stops << JET_CLI_DAP_FRAME_BITS) + row)
    }

    // The frame `id` names at this stop; None when it names another stop's.
    frame_of: fn(self, id: Int) -> JetCLIDapFrame? Never! {
        if id < 0 || (id >> JET_CLI_DAP_FRAME_BITS) != self.stops -> return None
        row: id & ((1 << JET_CLI_DAP_FRAME_BITS) - 1)
        if row >= self.frames.len() -> return None
        Val(JetCLIDapFrame{task: self.frames[row].task, index: self.frames[row].index})
    }

    // Where `settled` left the program: what the run said on the way, then
    // `stopped` (for `reason` unless a breakpoint, a watch, its stopping
    // exit or a fault stopped it), or its end. A watch's stop is a `data
    // breakpoint` one, described by the change it saw; a stopping exit or a
    // fault is an `exception` one, described by its status or signal. The
    // stop is a new one: the frame ids and variable references of the last
    // name nothing.
    report: fn(&self, session: &NativeSession, settled: NativeSettled, reason: String) -[FS, IO, Time.Wait, FFI.Asm]> Never! {
        self.tell(session, settled.said)
        self.stops = (self.stops + 1) & (JET_CLI_DAP_STOPS - 1)
        self.frames = [JetCLIDapFrame]{}
        self.rows = [Int:Int]{}
        stop: settled.stop
        if stop.kind == {
            .Paused -> {
                self.task = session.stopped_task()
                hit: settled.hit
                watch: stop.reason.starts_with("watchpoint ")
                exiting: stop.reason.starts_with("exiting ")
                fault: stop.reason.starts_with("fault ")
                why: if {
                    watch -> "data breakpoint"
                    exiting || fault -> "exception"
                    hit != None -> "breakpoint"
                    else -> reason
                }
                ids: if hit == .Val(number) -> ",\"hitBreakpointIds\":[{number}]" else -> ""
                change: if {
                    watch -> ",\"hitBreakpointIds\":[{stop.reason.after("watchpoint ")}],\"description\":{foundation_json_quote(session.watched)}"
                    exiting -> ",\"description\":{foundation_json_quote("Program exiting with status {stop.code}")}"
                    fault -> ",\"description\":{foundation_json_quote("Program received {stop.reason.after("fault ")}")}"
                    else -> ""
                }
                self.event("stopped", "{{\"reason\":\"{why}\",\"threadId\":{self.task},\"allThreadsStopped\":true{ids}{change}}}")
            }
            .Exited -> {
                self.event("exited", "{{\"exitCode\":{stop.code}}}")
                self.event("terminated", "{{}}")
            }
            .Signaled -> {
                self.event("output", "{{\"category\":\"stderr\",\"output\":{foundation_json_quote("Program stopped by {stop.reason}\n")}}}")
                self.event("terminated", "{{}}")
            }
        }
    }

    // What a run said on the way (`said`: the program's output, logpoints'
    // messages, failed conditions), then the program's new output.
    tell: fn(&self, session: &NativeSession, said: [NativeSaid]) -[FS, IO, Time.Wait]> Never! {
        loop line in said {
            self.event("output", "{{\"category\":\"{line.category}\",\"output\":{foundation_json_quote(line.text)}}}")
        }
        output: session.take_output()
        if output != "" {
            self.event("output", "{{\"category\":\"stdout\",\"output\":{foundation_json_quote(output)}}}")
        }
    }

    // A run the native debugger could not finish ends the session.
    stopped_by: fn(&self, failure: NativeDebugError) -[IO, Time.Wait]> Never! {
        self.event("output", "{{\"category\":\"stderr\",\"output\":{foundation_json_quote("{failure.detail}\n")}}}")
        self.event("terminated", "{{}}")
    }

    respond: fn(&self, request: JetCLIDapRequest, body: String) -[IO, Time.Wait]> Never! {
        self.seq += 1
        jet_cli_dap_send("{{\"seq\":{self.seq},\"type\":\"response\",\"request_seq\":{request.seq},\"success\":true,\"command\":{foundation_json_quote(request.command)},\"body\":{body}}}")
    }

    fail: fn(&self, request: JetCLIDapRequest, message: String) -[IO, Time.Wait]> Never! {
        self.seq += 1
        jet_cli_dap_send("{{\"seq\":{self.seq},\"type\":\"response\",\"request_seq\":{request.seq},\"success\":false,\"command\":{foundation_json_quote(request.command)},\"message\":{foundation_json_quote(message)}}}")
    }

    // The file the launch configuration `members` names in `stdin`, which
    // the program reads as its standard input from the start of each run,
    // as `jet debug --stdin=FILE` gives it; `/dev/null` without one, so the
    // program's reads end at once. None once `request` is refused: a
    // `stdin` that is no path is E2236, a file that can't be read E2105,
    // and the adapter's own stdin, which carries the protocol, E2102.
    stdin_of: fn(&self, request: JetCLIDapRequest, members: [{key: String, value: Dyn}]) -[FS, IO, Time.Wait]> String? {
        loop member in members {
            if member.key != "stdin" -> next
            path := ""
            if member.value == .Text(text) -> path = text
            if path == "" {
                self.refuse(request, NATIVE_ATTACH_INVALID, "field stdin must be the path of the file the program reads")
                return None
            }
            if !dap_files.can_read(path) {
                self.refuse_with(request, diagnostic_from_registry("E2105", None, "couldn't open `{path}`, the program's standard input", jet_cli_why("E2105"), "name a readable file in the launch configuration's `stdin`, or drop it"))
                return None
            }
            if dap_files.samefile(path, "/dev/stdin") ?? false {
                self.refuse_with(request, diagnostic_from_registry("E2102", None, "`stdin` names the adapter's own stdin, which carries the protocol", jet_cli_why("E2102"), "name another file in the launch configuration's `stdin`"))
                return None
            }
            return Val(path)
        }
        Val("/dev/null")
    }

    // `request`, refused with the registered diagnostic `code` and its
    // `detail` (refuse_with).
    refuse: fn(&self, request: JetCLIDapRequest, code: String, detail: String) -[IO, Time.Wait]> Never! {
        self.refuse_with(request, native_debug_report(code, detail))
    }

    // `request`, refused with `report`: the DAP error of its code (E2236
    // jet.invalidArguments, E2238 jet.staleReference, any other
    // jet.unavailable), whose format is the report's What and whose
    // `jetCode` is the code.
    refuse_with: fn(&self, request: JetCLIDapRequest, report: Diagnostic) -[IO, Time.Wait]> Never! {
        error := {name: "jet.unavailable", id: 22034}
        if report.code == NATIVE_ATTACH_INVALID -> error = {name: "jet.invalidArguments", id: 22032}
        if report.code == JET_CLI_DAP_STALE -> error = {name: "jet.staleReference", id: 22036}
        self.seq += 1
        jet_cli_dap_send("{{\"seq\":{self.seq},\"type\":\"response\",\"request_seq\":{request.seq},\"success\":false,\"command\":{foundation_json_quote(request.command)},\"message\":\"{error.name}\",\"body\":{{\"error\":{{\"id\":{error.id},\"format\":{foundation_json_quote(report.what)},\"showUser\":true,\"variables\":{{\"jetCode\":\"{report.code}\"}}}}}}}}")
    }

    event: fn(&self, name: String, body: String) -[IO, Time.Wait]> Never! {
        self.seq += 1
        jet_cli_dap_send("{{\"seq\":{self.seq},\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"{name}\",\"body\":{body}}}")
    }
}

// Answer requests until stdin ends or the editor disconnects: those that
// waited for a stop first, then the next on stdin. `fix` compiles `entry`
// with `deep_checks`, as the program's build did, when it is `fixable`.
jet_cli_debug_dap: fn(session: &NativeSession, entry: String, deep_checks: DeepChecks, fixable: Bool{false}) -[FS, Env, Exec, IO, Net, Time, FFI.Asm]> Never! {
    dap := JetCLIDap{seq: 0, stop_on_entry: false, args: [String]{}, placed: [String:[Int]]{}, launched: false, fixable: fixable}
    loop !dap.done {
        request := JetCLIDapRequest{seq: 0, command: "", arguments: [{key: String, value: Dyn}]{}}
        if dap.waiting.len() > 0 {
            // The first that waited.
            dap.waiting.reverse()
            request = dap.waiting.pop() ?? break
            dap.waiting.reverse()
        } else {
            if dap.ended -> break
            text: jet_cli_dap_read() ?? break
            request = jet_cli_dap_request(text)
        }
        if request.command == "disconnect" {
            session.close()
            dap.respond(request, "{{}}")
            break
        }
        dap.handle(session, request.move(), entry, deep_checks)
    }
}

// `jet debug --dap` when its session can't begin (a replay of a recording
// of other source, E3621, or another recording or replay refused before
// the program loads): `initialize` is answered, then every other request
// is refused with `report`, its code the error's `jetCode`, and the first
// refusal ends the session for the editor (`terminated`); `disconnect`
// ends the adapter, as the end of stdin does.
jet_cli_dap_refused: fn(report: Diagnostic) -[IO, Time.Wait]> Never! {
    dap := JetCLIDap{seq: 0, stop_on_entry: false, args: [String]{}, placed: [String:[Int]]{}, launched: false}
    ended := false
    loop {
        text: jet_cli_dap_read() ?? break
        request: jet_cli_dap_request(text)
        if request.command == {
            "initialize" -> {
                dap.respond(request, "{{\"supportsConfigurationDoneRequest\":true}}")
            }
            "disconnect" -> {
                dap.respond(request, "{{}}")
                break
            }
            else -> {
                dap.refuse_with(request, report)
                if !ended {
                    ended = true
                    dap.event("terminated", "{{}}")
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

// The next message's JSON text: a header block naming its `Content-Length`,
// then that many bytes. None at the end of stdin. Standard input is read a
// byte at a time up to the body, so no read waits on bytes the editor has not
// sent.
jet_cli_dap_read: fn() -[IO, Time.Wait]> String? Never! {
    input := dap_term.stdin()
    length := -1
    header := [U8]{}
    loop true {
        byte: input.read_bytes(1) ?? return None
        if byte.len() == 0 -> return None
        if byte[0] != 10 {
            header.push(byte[0])
            next
        }
        line: (String.from_bytes(header) ?? "").trim()
        header = [U8]{}
        if line == "" && length >= 0 -> break
        if line.to_lower().starts_with("content-length:") {
            length = Int.parse(line.after(":").trim()) ?? -1
        }
    }
    body := [U8]{}
    loop body.len() < length {
        chunk: input.read_bytes(length - body.len()) ?? return None
        if chunk.len() == 0 -> return None
        body.extend(chunk)
    }
    Val(String.from_bytes(body) ?? return None)
}

jet_cli_dap_send: fn(json: String) -[IO, Time.Wait]> Never! {
    jet_cli_debug_write("Content-Length: {json.bytes().len()}\r\n\r\n{json}")
}

// The request `text` holds; a request that is not a JSON object has no
// command, and is answered as an unknown one.
jet_cli_dap_request: fn(text: String) -> JetCLIDapRequest Never! {
    request := JetCLIDapRequest{seq: 0, command: "", arguments: [{key: String, value: Dyn}]{}}
    parsed: dap_json.parse(text) ?? return request
    fields := jet_cli_dap_members(parsed.move())
    loop fields.len() > 0 {
        field := fields.pop() ?? break
        if field.key == {
            "seq" -> request.seq = jet_cli_dap_number(field.value)
            "command" -> {
                if field.value.move() == .Text(name) -> request.command = name
                field.value = Dyn.Null
            }
            "arguments" -> {
                request.arguments = jet_cli_dap_members(field.value.move())
                field.value = Dyn.Null
            }
            else -> {}
        }
    }
    request
}

// The members of a JSON object, taken out of it; none for another value.
jet_cli_dap_members: fn(value: &&Dyn) -> [{key: String, value: Dyn}] Never! {
    if value.move() == {
        .Object(fields) -> fields
        .Null | .Bool(_) | .Int(_) | .Float(_) | .Number(_) | .Text(_) | .Bytes(_) | .DateTime(_) | .Array(_) -> [{key: String, value: Dyn}]{}
    }
}

// The strings of the array member `name`, in order, taken out of `members`.
jet_cli_dap_texts_of: fn(members: &&[{key: String, value: Dyn}], name: String) -> [String] Never! {
    fields := members.move()
    loop fields.len() > 0 {
        field := fields.pop() ?? break
        if field.key != name -> next
        items := if field.value.move() == {
            .Array(list) -> list
            .Null | .Bool(_) | .Int(_) | .Float(_) | .Number(_) | .Text(_) | .Bytes(_) | .DateTime(_) | .Object(_) -> [Dyn]{}
        }
        field.value = Dyn.Null
        items.reverse()
        texts := [String]{}
        loop items.len() > 0 {
            item: items.pop() ?? break
            if item.move() == .Text(text) -> texts.push(text)
        }
        return texts
    }
    [String]{}
}

// The members of the object member `name`, taken out of `members`; none
// when it has none.
jet_cli_dap_object_of: fn(members: &&[{key: String, value: Dyn}], name: String) -> [{key: String, value: Dyn}] Never! {
    fields := members.move()
    loop fields.len() > 0 {
        field := fields.pop() ?? break
        if field.key == name -> return jet_cli_dap_members(field.value.move())
    }
    [{key: String, value: Dyn}]{}
}

// The integer `value` holds, or -1. A parsed JSON number is a `.Number`
// lexeme, which foundation_json_integer reads.
jet_cli_dap_number: fn(value: Dyn) -> Int Never! { foundation_json_integer(value) ?? -1 }

// The integer member `name`, or -1.
jet_cli_dap_int: fn(members: [{key: String, value: Dyn}], name: String) -> Int Never! {
    loop member in members {
        if member.key == name -> return jet_cli_dap_number(member.value)
    }
    -1
}

// The boolean member `name`, or false.
jet_cli_dap_bool: fn(members: [{key: String, value: Dyn}], name: String) -> Bool Never! {
    loop member in members {
        if member.key == name && member.value == .Bool(flag) -> return flag
    }
    false
}

// The string member `name`, or "".
jet_cli_dap_string: fn(members: [{key: String, value: Dyn}], name: String) -> String Never! {
    loop member in members {
        if member.key == name && member.value == .Text(text) -> return text
    }
    ""
}

// The integer member `name`, or 0 when it is absent or no integer: an
// offset DAP leaves optional.
jet_cli_dap_offset: fn(members: [{key: String, value: Dyn}], name: String) -> Int Never! {
    loop member in members {
        if member.key == name -> return foundation_json_integer(member.value) ?? 0
    }
    0
}

// The address a `memoryReference` names, as `instructionPointerReference`
// gives it (`0x401000`) or in decimal; None for any other text, or one
// past 15 hex digits.
jet_cli_dap_address: fn(text: String) -> Int? Never! {
    if !text.starts_with("0x") && !text.starts_with("0X") {
        return Val(Int.parse(text) ?? return None)
    }
    digits: text.slice(2, text.len())
    if digits.len() == 0 || digits.len() > 15 -> return None
    value := 0
    loop byte in digits.bytes() {
        digit: Int{byte}
        nibble: if {
            digit >= 48 && digit <= 57 -> digit - 48
            digit >= 97 && digit <= 102 -> digit - 87
            digit >= 65 && digit <= 70 -> digit - 55
            else -> {
                return None
            }
        }
        value = (value << 4) | nibble
    }
    Val(value)
}

// `threads`: each task of the stopped program by its id, named by its
// label, its id and its state, with what it waits on.
jet_cli_dap_threads: fn(session: &NativeSession) -> String NativeDebugError! {
    tasks: session.task_rows() ?? return Err(err)
    rows := [String]{}
    loop row in tasks {
        wait: if row.task.wait != "" && row.task.state != NATIVE_DEBUG_TASK_RUNNING -> ", {row.task.wait}" else -> ""
        name: "{row.task.label} (task {row.task.id}, {row.state}{wait})"
        rows.push("{{\"id\":{row.task.id},\"name\":{foundation_json_quote(name)}}}")
    }
    Ok("{{\"threads\":[{rows.join(",")}]}}")
}

// Whether the stopped thread has yet to run any of the program's own code:
// no machine frame of its stack lies in a function of the image, only in
// the runtime that starts the program.
jet_cli_dap_starting: fn(session: &NativeSession) -> Bool NativeDebugError! {
    session.focus = None
    machine: session.unwind() ?? return Err(err)
    loop (index, frame) in machine {
        if native_function_at(session.image, native_lookup(index, frame.pc)) != None {
            return Ok(false)
        }
    }
    Ok(true)
}

// The key of task `task`'s frame `index` among a stop's listed frames
// (JetCLIDap.rows): an index, a machine frame's from JET_CLI_DAP_RAW, is
// below twice JET_CLI_DAP_RAW.
jet_cli_dap_frame_key: fn(task: Int, index: Int) -> Int Never! {
    task * JET_CLI_DAP_RAW * 2 + index
}

// `variables` of the machine frame `index`'s `[raw] Locals`: its pc and
// canonical frame address.
jet_cli_dap_raw_variables: fn(session: &NativeSession, index: Int) -> String NativeDebugError! {
    machine: session.unwind() ?? return Err(err)
    if index < 0 || index >= machine.len() -> return Ok("{{\"variables\":[]}}")
    pc: "{{\"name\":\"pc\",\"value\":\"{native_debug_hex(machine[index].pc)}\",\"variablesReference\":0}}"
    cfa: "{{\"name\":\"cfa\",\"value\":\"{native_debug_hex(machine[index].cfa)}\",\"variablesReference\":0}}"
    Ok("{{\"variables\":[{pc},{cfa}]}}")
}

// The locals of frame `frame` (an index in the session's backtrace). The
// innermost frame stays selected, as stepping needs.
jet_cli_dap_frame_locals: fn(session: &NativeSession, frame: Int) -> [NativeLocal] NativeDebugError! {
    if frame > 0 -> _: session.select_frame(frame) ?? return Err(err)
    locals: session.locals() ?? return Err(err)
    if frame > 0 -> _: session.select_frame(0) ?? return Err(err)
    Ok(locals)
}

// `variables` of frame `frame`'s scope: its locals by name, with their Jet
// types; for a machine frame (from JET_CLI_DAP_RAW), its `[raw] Locals`.
jet_cli_dap_variables: fn(session: &NativeSession, frame: Int) -> String NativeDebugError! {
    if frame < 0 -> return Ok("{{\"variables\":[]}}")
    if frame >= JET_CLI_DAP_RAW {
        raw: jet_cli_dap_raw_variables(session, frame - JET_CLI_DAP_RAW) ?? return Err(err)
        return Ok(raw)
    }
    locals := jet_cli_dap_frame_locals(session, frame) ?? return Err(err)
    locals.sort_by(fn(left: NativeLocal, right: NativeLocal) { left.name <=> right.name })
    rows := [String]{}
    loop local in locals {
        rows.push("{{\"name\":{foundation_json_quote(local.name)},\"value\":{foundation_json_quote(local.value)},\"type\":{foundation_json_quote(local.type_name)},\"variablesReference\":0}}")
    }
    Ok("{{\"variables\":[{rows.join(",")}]}}")
}

// `evaluate`: `text` in frame `frame` (the innermost when the request names
// none), through the session's evaluator. The innermost frame stays
// selected, as stepping needs.
jet_cli_dap_evaluate: fn(session: &NativeSession, text: String, frame: Int) -[FS, Env, Exec, IO, Net, Time, FFI.Asm]> String NativeEvalRefused! {
    if frame > 0 {
        _: session.select_frame(frame) ?? return Err(NativeEvalRefused{message: err.detail})
    }
    shown := {text: "", type_name: ""}
    refusal := ""
    if session.evaluate(text) == {
        .Ok(value) -> { shown = {text: value.shown, type_name: value.type_name} }
        .Err(failure) -> refusal = failure.message
    }
    if frame > 0 -> _: session.select_frame(0) ?? return Err(NativeEvalRefused{message: err.detail})
    if refusal != "" -> return Err(NativeEvalRefused{message: refusal})
    Ok("{{\"result\":{foundation_json_quote(shown.text)},\"type\":{foundation_json_quote(shown.type_name)},\"variablesReference\":0}}")
}

// Watch `name` in frame `frame` (an index in the stopped task's backtrace),
// or, unless `place`, find only whether it can be watched there
// (NativeSession.watch). The innermost frame stays selected, as stepping
// needs.
jet_cli_dap_watch: fn(session: &NativeSession, name: String, frame: Int, place: Bool{true}) -[FS, Env, Exec, IO, Net, Time, FFI.Asm]> NativeWatched NativeDebugError! {
    if frame > 0 -> _: session.select_frame(frame) ?? return Err(err)
    found: session.watch(name, place: place) ?? return Err(err)
    if frame > 0 -> _: session.select_frame(0) ?? return Err(err)
    Ok(found)
}

// The stop, the frame index and the place a data id
// (`<stop>:<frame>:<name>`, dataBreakpointInfo's) names; -1 for a part it
// lacks.
jet_cli_dap_data_place: fn(id: String) -> {stop: Int, index: Int, name: String} Never! {
    rest: id.after(":")
    {stop: Int.parse(id.before(":")) ?? -1, index: Int.parse(rest.before(":")) ?? -1, name: rest.after(":")}
}

// `dataBreakpointInfo` of a place no watch can take: no data id, and
// E2237's What for `detail`, its `jetCode` naming the code.
jet_cli_dap_no_data: fn(detail: String) -> String Never! {
    report: native_debug_report(NATIVE_DEBUG_REFUSED, detail)
    "{{\"dataId\":null,\"description\":{foundation_json_quote(report.what)},\"jetCode\":\"{NATIVE_DEBUG_REFUSED}\"}}"
}

// One event of `events`: event `event`, the stop `reached` (none when it
// was not reached), `current` when the program is at it.
jet_cli_dap_event: fn(event: Int, reached: NativeStop?, current: Bool{false}) -> String Never! {
    place := ""
    reason := ""
    if reached == .Val(stop) {
        reason = ",\"reason\":{foundation_json_quote(stop.reason)}"
        if stop.frame == .Val(frame) {
            place = ",\"function\":{foundation_json_quote(frame.function)},\"file\":{foundation_json_quote(frame.file)},\"line\":{frame.line}"
        }
    }
    "{{\"event\":{event}{reason}{place},\"current\":{current}}}"
}

// A data breakpoint not placed, refused with the registered diagnostic
// `code` and its `detail`: its message the report's What, its `jetCode`
// the code.
jet_cli_dap_unverified: fn(code: String, detail: String) -> String Never! {
    report: native_debug_report(code, detail)
    "{{\"verified\":false,\"message\":{foundation_json_quote(report.what)},\"jetCode\":\"{code}\"}}"
}
